
  Consequence: any user who currently clicks that button loses the only way to get report data out of this page —
  there's no other export path in the repo. The removal is also silent: no deprecation notice, and a bookmark or doc
  pointing at it just finds the button gone. And since [38;5;153mexport.js[39m contains nothing but the handler, deleting the button
  means deleting the file and its [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag too, which is slightly wider than "a button and its handler."

  Nothing here is hard to bring back (it's one commit to revert), but "we don't use it anymore" is the part I can't
  verify from the code — the page ships to whoever loads it.

  Confirm and I'll delete all three pieces: the button, the script tag, and [38;5;153mexport.js[39m.

